<title>POLAND: Polish grain prices all lower last week.</title>
<headline>Polish grain prices all lower last week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement that wheat, rye and barley prices fell at last week's grain auctions after rising a week earlier.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to June 28    previous week    yr/yr change</p>
<p>   Wheat	51.00 zl/q	  52.10 zl/q	 -20.3 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  39.00 zl/q	  39.74 zl/q	  -4.9 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     46.00 zl/q	  46.74 zl/q	 -19.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
